00:09:06.076 --> 00:09:10.916
Lastly, native vector search.
So we have databases that support native vector search.

00:09:10.916 --> 00:09:17.876
So for those folks that are not familiar with vector search,
this basically means it's a search technique that converts data.

00:09:17.916 --> 00:09:22.316
This data can be text. This can be images, this can be videos.

00:09:22.636 --> 00:09:27.756
And we do have multi-modal embedding models
right now that can do a mixture of all of them.

00:09:28.116 --> 00:09:34.036
So this means that you can convert all
of those data into its numerical representation

00:09:34.316 --> 00:09:40.276
and do similar search based on mathematical distance instead of,
you know, basic keyword matching.

00:09:40.796 --> 00:09:48.796
So databases like Aurora, Postgres, RDS, Postgres, ElastiCache
for Val key, Neptune, OpenSearch, and as I mentioned earlier,

00:09:48.836 --> 00:09:51.076
S3 Vectors as well support this natively.

00:09:51.076 --> 00:09:58.156
So that means your AI agents can do RAG based type of queries
without you having to move your data to another database

00:09:58.156 --> 00:10:00.000
